<score-partwise>
  <work>
    <work-title>Lord As To Thy Dear Cross</work-title>
  </work>
  <identification>
    <creator type="composer">Words: John Hampden Gurney, 1838.
Music: 'St. Bernard (Richardson)' or 'St. Bernard (Tochter Sion)' from Tochter Sion, Cologne, 1741.
Setting: John Richardson, 1877.
copyright: public domain.  This score is a part of the Open Hymnal Project, 2026 Revision.</creator>
    <encoding>
      <encoder>abc2xml version 268</encoder>
      <software>https://wim.vree.org/svgParse/abc2xml.html</software>
      <encoding-date>2026-09-07</encoding-date>
    </encoding>
    <source>Music and Lyrics source: "The New Hymnal (Episcopal)", 1916 Hymn 125
the oldest copy of this arrangement that I can find is in "Church Hymnal", 1877 hymn 345 attributed to W. Richardson.  It's then in the Scottish Hymnal of 1892 as John Richardson.  I think the first was a misprint. I can't find a composer named W. Richardson in that era.</source>
  </identification>
